// Cardnull OS 2's letter shapes — the bitmap font the
// pixel face (Stone 9) is drawn with.
//
// The font is ours, drawn for this system and public
// domain like everything else in it: ninety-five shapes,
// one for each printable letter, figure, and mark of the
// common set (the codes 32 to 126), each eight pixels
// wide and eight tall, drawn at twice size on the screen
// (see pixface.nifla). Every shape stands below in the
// comments exactly as it is drawn — # is a lit pixel —
// and the numbers loaded beside it are its rows, one
// number a row, the leftmost pixel the row's high bit.
//
// fontload fills a block of bytes the main body hands it
// (768 bytes is enough): the shape for a letter stands at
// (its code - 32) * 8, eight row-bytes in order. The block
// is the font's only keeping; the drawing is pixface's.

// Loads every shape into the block handed in.
make fontload(block: bytes) {

    // ' ' (32)
    //   ........
    //   ........
    //   ........
    //   ........
    //   ........
    //   ........
    //   ........
    //   ........
    block[0] = 0
    block[1] = 0
    block[2] = 0
    block[3] = 0
    block[4] = 0
    block[5] = 0
    block[6] = 0
    block[7] = 0

    // '!' (33)
